==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|culpable|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|culpable|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|culpabilis||blameworthy|lang=la}}, from {{term|culpare||to blame, condemn}}, from {{term|culpa||fault, crime, mistake}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-culpable.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[merit|Meriting]] [[condemnation]], [[censure]] or [[blame]], especially as something [[wrong]], [[harmful]] or [[injurious]]; [[blameworthy]].
#: ''I am '''culpable''' for stealing your money.''

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|culpability}}
* {{l|en|culpably}}
* {{l|en|culpable homicide}}
* {{l|en|culpable negligence}}

